diff --git a/docs/configuration.md b/docs/configuration.md
index 71a932f..be14972 100644
--- a/docs/configuration.md
+++ b/docs/configuration.md
@@ -49,6 +49,39 @@ wins. Outputs are unaffected.
 
 The Gemma 4 vision sidecar sets `disable_chunked_mm_input` on the scheduler config so an image block stays inside one prefill step wherever the scheduler allows (the image-block rows need their whole block in the batch). A block that still ends up split falls back to causal attention for that request, with a `falling back to causal attention` warning; see [Supported Models](supported_models.md).
 
+## Per-request Whole-prompt Attention
+
+The MLX backend optionally accepts `vllm_xargs.attention_mode` on generation
+requests. Enable it explicitly with:
+
+```bash
+vllm serve /path/to/model \
+  --additional-config '{"bidirectional_attention": true}' \
+  --no-enable-prefix-caching --no-enable-chunked-prefill \
+  --mamba-cache-mode none \
+  --max-model-len 40960 --max-num-batched-tokens 40960
+```
+
+`"bidirectional"` computes attention over the complete prompt on full-attention
+SDPA layers only; sliding-window and recurrent/Gated DeltaNet layers retain their
+existing semantics. It requires `max_tokens=1`: this is a single-token readout,
+not bidirectional autoregressive generation. The prompt must fit within
+`max_model_len` with room for that token. Requests without the flag stay causal;
+`"causal"` explicitly selects that behavior. Aliases `one-way`, `one_way`,
+`oneway`, `two-way`, `two_way`, and `twoway` follow the same two modes.
+Invalid modes, disabled bidirectional requests and invalid readout lengths
+are API validation errors, not silent causal fallbacks.
+
+The opt-in requires unquantized KV (`--kv-cache-dtype auto`, no TurboQuant), the
+MLX backend, no prefix caching, no chunked prefill, Mamba cache mode `none`, and a
+batch token budget at least as large as `max_model_len`. It rejects speculative
+decoding, pipeline/tensor/data parallelism, KV transfer, pooling and MLA.
+These are explicit startup requirements; the plugin does not silently rewrite
+them. Causal requests on this engine consequently also forego prefix caching.
+The worker rejects any bidirectional cached-prefix, intermediate-chunk or decode
+work that nevertheless reaches execution. Existing image-block ranges remain
+request- and layer-scoped, including in mixed causal/bidirectional batches.
+
 ## Speculative Decoding
 
 Pass `--speculative-config` with a JSON object to enable speculative decoding.
